    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d764">

                <pb facs="0721" n="549" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg549"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111/4540</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Secretary of the
                        Treasury</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">McAdoo</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 19, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your letter of to-day’s date enclosing a copy of a communication,
                    dated February 17, from the collector of customs at Norfolk, in regard to the
                    British S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Oxonian</hi> which arrived at that port on
                    February 13 with armament mounted on board.</p>
                <p>In reply I beg to confirm my telephone conversation with your Department
                    authorizing the clearance of the <hi rendition="#italic">Oxonian</hi> upon the
                    filing of the assurance by the British Consul at Norfolk that the gun is for
                    defensive purposes only. The incident reported in the newspapers has been taken
                    up with British Embassy at this Capital, and a statement has been filed by the
                    British Ambassador, on the strength of which this Department is willing to waive
                    further inquiry at this time, but it is understood that the case is not to stand
                    as a precedent for future similar cases which are to be decided wholly on their
                    individual merits.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">William Phillips</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Assistant Secretary</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
